  "title": "Outside fields are incoherent to a brain tuned to its own",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "8a696c41-b7af-4c9d-bfe3-dc2513b2e106",
      "text": "Evolution and development tuned the brain to encode and decode its own field. Outside fields such as TMS or MRI are incoherent signals to it, able to disrupt thought but not to form coherent thoughts, and suitably structured fields such as TMS do influence thought.",
